            "slot": "s2355",
            "repere": "Texte · I've used foam rollers, stick rollers, a",
            "text": "I've used foam rollers, stick rollers, and deep tissue massage balls before. All worked ok but then I heard about this tool here: Rolflex. The name sounds gimicky but after watching a bunch of video reviews, I decided to give it a go. It just arrived an hour ago and after a few mins of use, Sweet Little Baby Jesus, I've finally got some instant relief! Used on my calves, thighs, shins, and quads that were all tight/sore from soccer injuries years ago. I was able to go deeper into the muscles and apply the right amount of pressure to each knot. My legs now feel like happy jelly and I'm able to move and rotate without stress or pain. 100% worth it! I'm still testing it out so I can't speak for the durability of it. But does it work: Yes and Yes.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
